---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout>
    <section>
        <div class="relative px-8 py-12 mx-auto md:px-12 lg:px-32 max-w-7xl lg:pb-24">
            <div class="text-center">
                <h1
                    class="text-5xl font-semibold font-display text-blue-950 sm:text-6xl text-balance w-3/4 mx-auto">
                    What is OnTrack? 
                </h1>
                

            </div>
            
            <p>OnTrack is a unit management system originally developed to support a task oriented approach to portfolio assessment, however it can support many different types of assessment models.
In OnTrack, students complete tasks to learn content, develop skills, and develop dispositions. They can submit them for feedback during the teaching period, and their assigned tutor can view the work and leave feedback. The student is able to submit the same task multiple times until it is judged acceptable, or until they exceed their feedback limit.
With OnTrack you can manage the content, sequence and submission dates for each task. You can manage the interactions with the students both online and in class, and you can manage the work of the staff assigned to the unit.

Students can choose their target grade, adjust their due dates and see a gantt chart of their progress through the tasks.</p>
        </div>
    </section>
</BaseLayout>
